The experimental seam is now fixed: five-fold anchor-disjoint cross-fitting; the same learned singleton head feeds the regression models; the baseline is an explicit sum of learned atomic pair terms; Alternative A implements the stated per-beam anchored finite-difference formula exactly; Alternative B is a RankNet-style comparator trained only on same-anchor candidate pairs. Selection uses nominal exact-score panels, while the primary outcome is re-evaluated under the frozen realised field as a ratio of pooled bits to pooled joules.
